From: terminusfilms <steve@terminusfilms.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:27:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Mount the open_geographies_platform engine (local path) +
 its two additive migrations

On top of ecds ff020c5 (open_geographies_fairdata at 67d0728, OpenGeographies::Engine
mounted). The platform engine's module is OpenGeographiesPlatform so the two engines
coexist; its routes are prepended ahead of the SPA catch-all.
---
 Gemfile                                       |  4 ++++
 Gemfile.lock                                  |  8 +++++++
 ...tor_search_collections.open_geographies.rb | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 ...e_data_connector_sites.open_geographies.rb | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 60 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 db/migrate/20260904212559_create_core_data_connector_search_collections.open_geographies.rb
 create mode 100644 db/migrate/20260904212560_create_core_data_connector_sites.open_geographies.rb

diff --git a/Gemfile b/Gemfile
index e63f61a..3ef6618 100644
--- a/Gemfile
+++ b/Gemfile
@@ -90,6 +90,10 @@ end
 # is pushed - this ref won't resolve against the renamed repo's history correctly
 # until then.
 gem 'open_geographies_fairdata', git: 'https://github.com/ecds/open-geographies-fairdata.git', ref: '67d0728'
+# Open Geographies platform engine (upper layer: wizard/provisioning, Sites, imports,
+# by-slug public atlas API). Depends on the FairData engine above at runtime; local
+# path while the two are developed side by side — becomes a git ref at integration.
+gem 'open_geographies_platform', path: '../open-geographies-engine'
 # Elasticserch
 gem 'elasticsearch', '~> 8.0'
 gem 'faraday-typhoeus', '~> 1.0' # Needed to use Elasticsearch in rake tasks.
